# .mailmap — map false-attribution authors to the canonical human identity.
#
# GitHub honors this file when rendering the Contributors graph + PR commit
# lists + blame views: any commit with the wrong-side identity will be
# displayed as the proper-side identity, even though the raw SHA stays
# unchanged. This is the standard fix for "Claude Code committed with author
# Claude <claude@anthropic.com> but the work was actually done on behalf of
# the human user via the user's agent runtime (OpenCode + MiniMax-M3 here)".
#
# Format (each line):
#   Proper Name <proper@email>  <wrong@email>          # short form (keeps wrong name)
#   Proper Name <proper@email>  Wrong Name <wrong@em>  # full form

# Claude Code's hardcoded author identity → the user's primary human identity.
# 3 commits on main with this author (the `feat(lc-2026): end-to-end Leaving
# Cert pipeline working` series) — they were authored when the user's
# workflow accidentally invoked Claude Code through scripts/claude-with-secrets.sh
# before that script was retired in the 2026-07-21-purge-claude-coauthor-trailer
# openspec change.
cianfhoghlaim <cianmacliathain@gmail.com> <claude@anthropic.com>
